# Vendored statement data of `Zeros0to1000`

Copied from `challenge/Zeros0to1000.lean` of `Garald1/zeta-zero-locations`
(the file Harald sent on 2026-11-08, sha256 `161dd725362204ad1fc7144493f54c6c81dc86ea47b7feb261d97037b01dc2fa`), with two changes only: the module-system
header (`module`, `public import Mathlib`, `@[expose] public section`) is
replaced by `import Mathlib.NumberTheory.LSeries.RiemannZeta` (the
definitions below need only `riemannZeta`; the light import keeps the
kernel checks of `Head1000Data` within memory), and the three theorems `located`, `unique`,
`count`, which that file states with `sorry`, are omitted. The definitions
below are unchanged. The three statements are restated, as one proposition,
by `Head1000.Certified` in `Head1000Table.lean`; nothing in this project
asserts them.

Original description: the location, to within 10^-20, of every zero of
Mathlib's `riemannZeta` with 0 < Im s <= 1000. `ordinates` lists, in
increasing order, the integers m_k nearest to 10^24 * gamma_k for the 649
zeros with 0 < Im rho <= 1000, as computed by Arb (acb_dirichlet_zeta_zeros,
160-bit ball arithmetic); the list is part of the statement, and no proof may
assume it is correct.
-/

